※ pl4g-test: compile=ok run=native,qemu exit=134 diag=none

※ A rotation puts back at the other end what a shift would have dropped, and
※ it turns the bits of the *type* rather than of the register the value is
※ held in: 13 as a byte is 0b0000_1101, and turned right by one it is
※ 0b1000_0110, which is 134.

let thirteen: u8 = 13u8
let one: u8 = 1u8

@[startup]
fn main() → u8:
    thirteen ↻ one
